# Schema of server.stxt, the configuration of a server of stxt-press (README.md, "Configuration").
# Each name has a single definition in the whole namespace. The values that the types do not check (a port above
# 65535, a folder that does not exist, a variable that is not set) are checked when the file is read.
Schema (@stxt.schema): dev.stxt.press
	Description: The configuration of a server of stxt-press: where it listens, its token, its resources and templates folders, which routes are on, its limits and the options of the templates. Relative paths are relative to the folder of the file.

	Node: Server
		Type: GROUP
		Description: The configuration of the server. Every child is optional: what is not written has its default.
		Children:
			Child: Host
				Max: 1
			Child: Port
				Max: 1
			Child: Token env
				Max: 1
			Child: Lazy init
				Max: 1
			Child: Warm up
				Max: 1
			Child: Resource folder
				Max: 1
			Child: Font folder
				Max: 1
			Child: Image folder
			Child: Template folder
				Max: 1
			Child: Routes
				Max: 1
			Child: Limits
				Max: 1
			Child: Template options
				Max: 1
			Child: Producer
				Max: 1
	Node: Host
		Type: INLINE
		Description: The address the server listens on. By default 127.0.0.1, only this machine; 0.0.0.0 for every address of the machine.
	Node: Port
		Type: NATURAL
		Description: The port, from 0 to 65535; 0 for any free one. By default 8080.
	Node: Token env
		Type: INLINE
		Description: The name of the environment variable that holds the token of the server: every route but /health then asks for Authorization: Bearer <token>. The variable has to be set and not empty when the server starts. Without Token env, the server asks for no token.
	Node: Lazy init
		Type: BOOLEAN
		Description: Whether the resources are opened when the first request needs them instead of when the server starts, without warm up. By default false, so that resources that are missing are seen before the first request.
	Node: Warm up
		Type: BOOLEAN
		Description: Whether the server warms up before answering: it reads the whole resources folder and converts every template with its sample data, to PDF and to SVG, so that the first request is as fast as the next ones. Until it ends, every request, /health too, is answered with 503 (SERVER_STARTING). A template that cannot be converted is a warning in the log. By default true, and false with Lazy init: true; both true is an error.
	Node: Resource folder
		Type: INLINE
		Description: The resources folder, with the fonts in fonts/ and the images in images/. By default resources, next to this file. Not with Font folder or Image folder.
	Node: Font folder
		Type: INLINE
		Description: The folder of the fonts, instead of the fonts/ of a Resource folder.
	Node: Image folder
		Type: INLINE
		Description: A folder of images, instead of the images/ of a Resource folder: the one of the paths without prefix, or, with Prefix, the one of the paths that start with it. Several, each with a different prefix.
		Children:
			Child: Prefix
				Max: 1
	Node: Prefix
		Type: INLINE
		Description: The first segments of the paths of the images of the folder: with logos, Image: logos/a.png is its file a.png.
	Node: Template folder
		Type: INLINE
		Description: The templates folder of /print and /templates. Without it, the server has no templates.
	Node: Producer
		Type: INLINE
		Description: The software that the PDFs of the server and of the commands render and print name as their producer, in their document information and their XMP. By default stxt-press and stxt-pdf with their versions, such as stxt-press 0.1.0 (stxt-pdf 0.16.0).

	Node: Routes
		Type: GROUP
		Description: Which routes are on, besides /print, /schema, /fonts and /health, which always are. A route that is off answers 404.
		Children:
			Child: Editor
				Max: 1
			Child: Render
				Max: 1
			Child: Templates
				Max: 1
	Node: Editor
		Type: BOOLEAN
		Description: Whether the index (GET /) and the web editor (GET /editor and /editor/{path}) are on, with their files under /assets/ and /fonts, which only the previews of the editor use. The pages are served without token; they ask for the token when the API answers 401. By default true.
	Node: Render
		Type: BOOLEAN
		Description: Whether POST /render, which converts any document, is on. By default true.
	Node: Templates
		Type: BOOLEAN
		Description: Whether /templates, which shows the texts and the sample data of the templates, is on. By default true.

	Node: Limits
		Type: GROUP
		Description: The limits of the server and of the engine. Each one is at least 1.
		Children:
			Child: Max body size
				Max: 1
			Child: Timeout
				Max: 1
			Child: Concurrent conversions
				Max: 1
			Child: Max pages
				Max: 1
			Child: Max image pixels
				Max: 1
			Child: Max SVG elements
				Max: 1
			Child: Max SVG depth
				Max: 1
			Child: Max PDF bytes
				Max: 1
	Node: Max body size
		Type: NATURAL
		Description: The largest body of a request, in bytes. By default 2097152 (2 MiB).
	Node: Timeout
		Type: NATURAL
		Description: The seconds a PDF or SVG conversion has: then it is cancelled and answered with 503. By default 30.
	Node: Concurrent conversions
		Type: NATURAL
		Description: How many PDF or SVG conversions run at once: one more is answered with 503 at once. By default 4.
	Node: Max pages
		Type: NATURAL
		Description: The pages of a document. By default 2000, the one of the engine.
	Node: Max image pixels
		Type: NATURAL
		Description: The pixels of a PNG or JPEG image. By default 25000000, the one of the engine.
	Node: Max SVG elements
		Type: NATURAL
		Description: The elements of an SVG image. By default 20000, the one of the engine.
	Node: Max SVG depth
		Type: NATURAL
		Description: The nesting of the elements of an SVG image. By default 64, the one of the engine.
	Node: Max PDF bytes
		Type: NATURAL
		Description: The size of a PDF image, in bytes. By default 20000000, the one of the engine.

	Node: Template options
		Type: GROUP
		Description: The options of the engine for every template of /print, the same as the options of a body of /render.
		Children:
			Child: PDF UA
				Max: 1
			Child: PDF A
				Max: 1
			Child: Exclude
	Node: PDF UA
		Type: ENUM
		Description: The part of PDF/UA the PDF complies with: 1 (PDF 1.7, by default) or 2 (PDF 2.0). 2 is not valid with PDF A.
		Values:
			Value: 1
			Value: 2
	Node: PDF A
		Type: ENUM
		Description: The PDF/A the PDF complies with besides: A2B, A2A, A3B or A3A. By default none.
		Values:
			Value: A2B
			Value: A2A
			Value: A3B
			Value: A3A
	Node: Exclude
		Type: ENUM
		Description: A check of the engine that is not made. One Exclude for each.
		Values:
			Value: CONTRAST
			Value: PDF_IMAGE_FONTS
			Value: PDF_IMAGE_ANNOTATIONS
			Value: BARCODE_SIZE
